<p>SessionEnd is where you clean up and report results. Generate a summary of what was done, send it to stakeholders, archive logs for auditing, delete temporary files.</p>
<p>This is useful for compliance. If your workflow touches production or sensitive data, SessionEnd lets you ensure all audit trails are preserved before the session closes.</p>
<h2 id="section-7">Notification: Fire and Forget External Communication</h2>
<p>Send data to external systems. Slack, email, webhooks—doesn't matter. This hook fires independently and doesn't block the session.</p>
