<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">  "action"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: {</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">    "read_state"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: {</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">      "file"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: </span><span style="--shiki-dark:#96D0FF;--shiki-light:#032F62">".hook-state.json"</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">    }</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">  }</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">}</span></span></code></pre></figure>
<p>Now both hooks can read the same state file.</p>
<h3 id="section-10">Trap 2: Async Wait Timeouts in Long-Running Tasks</h3>
<p>If your hook makes an async call (API request, database query, CI status check), Claude Code will wait. But only for a configurable limit. Exceed it and the session times out.</p>
<p>I wrote a hook to wait for CI to finish after a git push. 30 seconds in the test repo, no problem. On a real project with a 20-minute CI pipeline, the session timed out.</p>
<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=""><pre tabindex="0" data-language="json" data-theme="github-dark-dimmed github-light"><code data-language="json" data-theme="github-dark-dimmed github-light" style="display: grid;"><span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">{</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">  "hook_type"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: </span><span style="--shiki-dark:#96D0FF;--shiki-light:#032F62">"PostToolUse"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">,</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">  "event"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: </span><span style="--shiki-dark:#96D0FF;--shiki-light:#032F62">"git"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">,</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">  "action"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: {</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">    "wait_for_ci_completion"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: {</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">      "poll_interval"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: </span><span style="--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF;--shiki-light:#005CC5">10</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">,</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">      "max_wait_seconds"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: </span><span style="--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF;--shiki-light:#005CC5">300</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">,</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">      "on_timeout"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: </span><span style="--shiki-dark:#96D0FF;--shiki-light:#032F62">"continue_async"</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">    }</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">  }</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">}</span></span></code></pre></figure>
<p>The <code>on_timeout</code> action is critical. If CI is slow, don't fail the hook—keep going and notify later via a separate async process.</p>
<p>Another approach: split the work. PreToolUse triggers the CI build. PostToolUse checks if it's done, but doesn't wait. A separate background job checks later and notifies.</p>
<p>If it's the literal <code>command timed out</code> failure you're chasing rather than the design, I walk through the timeout setting and splitting long work in <a href="/articles/claude-code/claude-code-hook-command-timed-out-fix">When a Claude Code hook fails with "command timed out"</a>.</p>
<h3 id="section-11">Trap 3: Hook Interdependency Loops</h3>
<p>Complex setups use multiple hooks, each feeding output to the next. But if the dependencies form a loop, you get infinite recursion.</p>
<p>Real bug I hit:</p>
<ul>
<li>UserPromptSubmit transforms "git push" → "git push -f"</li>
<li>PreToolUse detects "-f" is risky, transforms back to "git push"</li>
<li>PostToolUse sees failure, tries "git push -f" again</li>
<li>PreToolUse blocks again</li>
<li>Loop forever</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Solution</strong>: Explicitly mark which keys each hook owns. Prevent one hook from undoing another's work.</p>
<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=""><pre tabindex="0" data-language="json" data-theme="github-dark-dimmed github-light"><code data-language="json" data-theme="github-dark-dimmed github-light" style="display: grid;"><span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">{</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">  "hook_type"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: </span><span style="--shiki-dark:#96D0FF;--shiki-light:#032F62">"UserPromptSubmit"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">,</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">  "output_key"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: </span><span style="--shiki-dark:#96D0FF;--shiki-light:#032F62">"user_input_raw"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">,</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">  "protected_keys"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: [</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#96D0FF;--shiki-light:#032F62">"validation_state"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">, </span><span style="--shiki-dark:#96D0FF;--shiki-light:#032F62">"retry_count"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">]</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">}</span></span></code></pre></figure>
<figure data-rehype-pretty-code-figure=""><pre tabindex="0" data-language="json" data-theme="github-dark-dimmed github-light"><code data-language="json" data-theme="github-dark-dimmed github-light" style="display: grid;"><span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">{</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">  "hook_type"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: </span><span style="--shiki-dark:#96D0FF;--shiki-light:#032F62">"PreToolUse"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">,</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">  "input_key"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: </span><span style="--shiki-dark:#96D0FF;--shiki-light:#032F62">"user_input_raw"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">,</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">  "output_key"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: </span><span style="--shiki-dark:#96D0FF;--shiki-light:#032F62">"command_validated"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">,</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#8DDB8C;--shiki-light:#005CC5">  "check_protected_keys"</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">: </span><span style="--shiki-dark:#6CB6FF;--shiki-light:#005CC5">true</span></span>
<span data-line=""><span style="--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7;--shiki-light:#24292E">}</span></span></code></pre></figure>
<p>Each hook declares: "I read from X, I write to Y, don't touch Z." That prevents loops.</p>
<p>The specific case where PostToolUse re-fires on its own output has its own writeup with a reproduction and fix: <a href="/articles/claude-code/claude-code-hooks-infinite-loop-fix">When Claude Code Hooks loop forever — stopping PostToolUse from self-triggering</a>.</p>
<h2 id="section-12">Ready-to-Use Templates</h2>
